<!-- Status-bar icon for household-activity notifications, and the app's mark.

     Android draws a notification small icon from its alpha channel alone and
     tints the result, so this must be a flat white-on-transparent silhouette.
     Pointing the plugin at @mipmap/ic_launcher instead would render as a solid
     white blob on Android 5+, which is why this exists as its own drawable
     rather than reusing the launcher artwork.

     The mark is a house whose lower half is a receipt with a torn bottom edge:
     the roof says household, the tear says expense. A plain receipt read as a
     generic document, and a generic status-bar icon is indistinguishable from
     every other app's.

     One outer subpath traces the whole silhouette — right roof slope, eave,
     body, tear, left eave, closing left slope — and two inner subpaths that
     evenOdd carves back out as the printed lines. evenOdd rather than winding
     order so the holes do not depend on the direction each rectangle happens to
     be drawn in; supported from API 24, which is this app's minSdk.

     ic_launcher_foreground.xml repeats this path data at launcher scale. Vector
     drawables cannot share a path between files, so the two are kept in sync by
     hand: change one, change the other, or the app icon and the notification it
     posts stop being the same mark. -->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24">
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:fillType="evenOdd"
        android:pathData="M12,1.6 L22,9.6 L19,9.6 L19,22.4 L17.25,19.9 L15.5,22.4 L13.75,19.9 L12,22.4 L10.25,19.9 L8.5,22.4 L6.75,19.9 L5,22.4 L5,9.6 L2,9.6 Z M7.6,12.4 L16.4,12.4 L16.4,14 L7.6,14 Z M7.6,16.4 L13.4,16.4 L13.4,18 L7.6,18 Z" />
</vector>
